{"id": "EUVD-2026-32216", "enisaUuid": "3ef36653-6005-346f-9591-b9e5366b1f45", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Fix tcx/netkit detach permissions when prog fd isn't given\n\nThis commit fixes a security issue where BPF_PROG_DETACH on tcx or\nnetkit devices could be executed by any user when no program fd was\nprovided, bypassing permission checks. The fix adds a capability\ncheck for CAP_NET_ADMIN or CAP_SYS_ADMIN in this case.", "datePublished": "2026-05-27T12:17:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:40:59", "baseScore": 7.3, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8e1623e7d61faf16cbadc80550da874303611ff5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0c249f523175963b0a746bba673ecebdf6cefd86", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4e0772cded109c238411f2fac36ac39302758b81", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3f04cc1e5374da4c5e791ae010a06cfea7bacbe6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ae23bc81ddf7c17b663c4ed1b21e35527b0a7131"], "aliases": ["GHSA-p87w-4q4g-fjpw", "CVE-2026-45932"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0889ed31-e83b-3d4f-99ab-8930ace2fd66", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e420bed025071a623d2720a92bc2245c84757ecb <0c249f523175963b0a746bba673ecebdf6cefd86"}, {"id": "14eaa8de-075a-3141-b486-691dddc9aa4f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e420bed025071a623d2720a92bc2245c84757ecb <ae23bc81ddf7c17b663c4ed1b21e35527b0a7131"}, {"id": "17cb3e32-77d2-34ee-8165-9699a99b95f3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0"}, {"id": "1aa2dac8-af8d-35c5-9df8-c47ff5d2ebf6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e420bed025071a623d2720a92bc2245c84757ecb <4e0772cded109c238411f2fac36ac39302758b81"}, {"id": "1bd450c3-9005-39a4-a488-71ab3